// The companion to saluta.exsc.
//
// `saluta` is pure and therefore cannot print. This is what printing looks
// like when authority has to be declared.
//
// Note what the row is NOT: it is not `poscit archivum`. The authority comes
// from the writer that was handed in, so this function requires exactly what
// its `Scriptor` requires and nothing more (§4.2 -- rows travel with the
// value's type). Point it at a file-backed writer and it needs the
// filesystem; point it at an in-memory one and it needs nothing at all. The
// function does not get to decide, and does not have to guess.

publica functio imprime_gutenbergio(s: Scriptor, t: textus) -> mensura poscit sicut s {
    redde s.scribe(t);
}

// Usage, and where the authority actually gets declared:
//
//     publica functio principium(a: archivum) -> mensura poscit archivum {
//         firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
//         redde imprime_gutenbergio(s, saluta());
//     }
//
// `poscit archivum` appears once, at the boundary, on the function that
// genuinely has the authority. §10.3's audit reads it straight out of the
// interface.
